Description: This package provides code to faciliate creation of the 2020 American
    Cancer Society (ACS) Guideline for Cancer Prevention Score and 2022 ACS Guideline 
    Score for Cancer Survivors. The ACS Guideline Scores evaluate lifestyle 
    factors associated with cancer risk and cancer survival. The score consists of 
    4 subcomponents - body mass index, physical activity, diet, and alcohol intake. 
    Each component is derived and scaled from 0-2, then summed together to create 
    the total ACS Guideline Score. The total ACS Guideline Score ranges from 0-8, 
    with higher scores indicating better alignment to the ACS Guidelines.
